<article class="env-exercise" id="03V9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03V9">Exercise <span data-tag="03V9">64.23.2</span>.</a> Let $\alpha _1, \ldots , \alpha _ n \in \mathbf{C}$. Then for any conic sector containing the positive real axis of the form $C_\varepsilon = \{  z \in \mathbf{C} \  | \  |\arg z| < \varepsilon \} $ with $\varepsilon > 0$, there exists an integer $k \geq 1$ such that $\alpha _1^ k, \ldots , \alpha _ n^ k \in C_\varepsilon $. </p>
